id: pm-d30cmk
title: "GH-799: confine custom item-type storage folders to the tracker root"
description: Enforce a platform-correct storage boundary for custom item-type folders before schema persistence and at runtime consumption. Reject any normalized or persisted folder that resolves outside the active tracker root while retaining valid nested relative folders and established contained absolute-looking compatibility.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[5]: "area:schema","area:security",github-report,path-safety,storage-boundary
created_at: "2026-07-28T18:19:50.185Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T18:57:13.827Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T18:38:22.832Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: schema add-type rejects every relative traversal that resolves outside the tracker root before writing schema/types.json; valid nested folders and established contained absolute-looking values remain supported; create cannot consume a legacy malicious persisted definition to write outside the tracker; POSIX and Windows path semantics have direct negative controls; CLI SDK contracts docs and exact 100% coverage remain green; isolated installed-package reproduction proves no artifact is created outside the tracker
parent: pm-8jdc
risk: critical
confidence: 95
reporter: github-issue-799
severity: critical
repro_steps: "Register a custom type whose storage folder normalizes outside the tracker boundary, then attempt to create an item of that type in an isolated workspace."
resolution: "Implemented one shared containment primitive across schema persistence, existing project definitions, and extension registrations; added unit, CLI integration, installed-package, documentation, and exact coverage proof."
expected_result: All custom type storage paths remain confined beneath the active tracker root and invalid definitions fail with actionable usage errors before any item or history write.
actual_result: "Custom item-type folders are canonicalized to portable tracker-relative paths at authoring and runtime registry consumption; escaping, drive-prefixed, empty, and NUL-bearing definitions fail before item or history writes."
fixed_version: 2026.7.28
component: "schema:item-type-storage"
customer_impact: "Untrusted schema customization can violate workspace isolation, split authoritative item state, and bypass the tracker/version-control boundary."
